<title>CHILE: Chile's Entel, Ericsson in deal.</title>
<headline>Chile's Entel, Ericsson in deal.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's largest long-distance provider Entel Chile SA said it has signed a $106 million contract with Sweden's Telefon AB L.M. Ericsson to install a mobile personal telephone network throughout the country.</p>
<p>The network is due to come into operation next year, said Entel in a statement.</p>
<p>Entel is around 20 percent owned by Italian telecom Stet SpA.</p>
<p>Ericsson signed a contract last month to upgrade the mobile telephone network of rival Chilean carrier Startel.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
</text>
